P(X = k) = \binom{10}{k} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{10}
\] where $\binom{10}{k}$ is the binomial coefficient, the number of ways to choose $k$ heads out of 10 flips. We need to calculate the sum of the probabilities for $k = 8, 9, 10$: \[
P(X \geq 8) = P(X = 8) + P(X = 9) + P(X = 10) = \binom{10}{8} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{10} + \binom{10}{9} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{10} + \binom{10}{10} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{10}
\] Simplifying, we get: \[
P(X \geq 8) = \left(\binom{10}{8} + \binom{10}{9} + \binom{10}{10}\right) \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{10} = \left(\frac{45 + 10 + 1}{1024}\right) = \frac{56}{1024} = \frac{7}{128}
\] </think> <answer> $\boxed{\frac{7}{128}}$ </answer>

